  "rationale": "All nine exact panels inspected. KP5 and KP6 retain amber eye slits: ordinary bilateral closure is therefore used rather than fully closed smile-lash contours. Deep bilateral narrowing, asymmetric brow relaxation, broad sealed width and independently biased positive corners must work together as a smug cat smile; a heavier-blink EXP102 alone is insufficient. KP6 is an eased peak; KP7 reopens eyes while its smaller smile lingers. Source head/body inclination is deliberately excluded. Canonical lip fullness and absent painted crease are disclosed appearance differences, not automatic rejection, but a generic smile cannot pass. Eye narrowing, source mouth bias and recovery must remain readable without a wink or full closure. No general open-width operation, new pigment, texture replacement, whole-mouth transform or profile registration."
